{"p":{"slug":"nicholas-robertson","first":"Nicholas","last":"Robertson","cc":"CHI","iso":"cl","country":"Chile","g":0,"img":"https://platform.worldofsailors.com/storage/uploads/2026/03/2-nicholas-robertson-1772897724.webp","cm":173,"kg":78,"bio":"Vigilant and proactive. Our Pitman does not miss one.\nBecause of his experience on different ships and positions, he is the ideal navigator for the Pitman position, as he is located in the nerve center of the ship. All the maneuvers pass through here (hoisting, lowering, giving the correct tension to each halyard according to the intensity of the wind, in addition to the rough ones).\nHe has been sailing in Optimist since he was 8 years old, participating in South American, North American and World Championships. He continued to compete in 420, Snipe, Lightning, J24, J105, Soto40, Oceanicos (ORC, IRC) and J70, where he obtained podium finishes in several national, world, and South American championships. He also has experience in offshore regattas (Fasnet, Caribean 600 and Transatlantic Race).\nHe is currently dedicated to sailing, mainly on J70, Lightning, Soto40 and J105. He is passionate and enjoys sailing (and life in general).","soc":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/nickrobertsonj/"},"rk":{"c":[8877,75.25,2780,"2026-11-24",[493,"2020-12-08"]]},"st":{"ev":40,"win":1,"pod":7,"avg":1.9,"best":1},"cls":["Snipe","ILCA 7","ILCA 6 (Open)","J/70","Etchells","Sunfish"],"recn":0},"res":{"s":[["2024-08-04","2024 Erie Open Regatta/Midwest Regional Championship I","Erie","USA","Sunfish","Regional",6,27,0,6],["2023-08-05","2023 I-LYA TS9","Erie","USA","ILCA 6 (Open)","Regional",2,17,0,5],["2023-07-30","2023 I-LYA TS8","Sandusky","USA","ILCA 6 (Open)","Regional",3,18,0,5],["2023-07-09","2023 USA Junior Olympics Sailing Festival - Lake Erie & I-LYA TS 6","Mentor","USA","ILCA 6 (Open)","National",2,37,0,5],["2023-06-24","2023 I-LYA TS5 Bob Sessions Memorial","Rocky River","USA","ILCA 6 (Open)","National",3,30,0,5],["2023-06-21"